{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "userdb-lev-2025-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.82: `userdb-lev-2025` -- `userdb-lev` at calendar year 2025 over a LEV database that keeps EVERY model-year group (`inputs/washtenaw-userdb-lev-all.esm`: MOVES5_MyLEVS_Template.sql unedited, all 92,274 emissionRateByAgeLEV rows). Same selection: THC, CO, NOx, NMHC and the PM2.5 group at running and start exhaust for 21, 31 and 32, every fuel MOVES adds, Washtenaw, DEFAULT domain, August, weekday, hour 7.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES beside `userdb-lev`: the LEV table's elemental-carbon and non-EC PM rows, which are at model-year group 45 (2025) and nowhere else, so only a run reaching model year 2025 reads them -- EC and NonECPM at model year 2025 read LEV rates, and the PM2.5 total, sulfate and aerosol water chained from them move with them; and the unedited template, the LEV tool's default. Execution database emissionRateByAge: 1,384,677 rows at the run's pollutant-processes, reproduced exactly by the merge in pandas, 92,274 of them the user's.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to the chain's `rateSurvivorCount`; `n_sourceBin` 2 and `n_physicsRow` 7 as in `userdb-lev`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "user-input-database",
      "lev"
    ]
  },
